---
description: Prefer nested entity refs (id + display name) over bare foreign-key IDs in API responses
alwaysApply: true
---

# API Entity Refs (users, merchants, …)

When an API response references another entity the UI may need to **display** (user, merchant, rider, …), do **not** return only a bare UUID.

## Prefer

```json
{
  "confirmedBy": { "id": "…", "name": "Alice Admin", "avatarUrl": null },
  "rejectedBy": null,
  "merchant": { "id": "…", "name": "Restaurant ABC", "logo": null }
}
```

## Avoid (for displayable refs)

```json
{
  "confirmedByUserId": "uuid-only",
  "rejectedByUserId": null
}
```

Bare IDs remain OK for **path params**, **request bodies**, filters, and internal joins — not as the sole representation of a related actor the front must label.

## Shared DTOs

Use the shared shapes in [`src/common/dto/entity-ref.dto.ts`](src/common/dto/entity-ref.dto.ts):

| Ref | Fields | Name source |
|-----|--------|-------------|
| `UserRefDto` | `id`, `name`, `avatarUrl` | `displayName` else `firstName + lastName` |
| `MerchantRefDto` | `id`, `name`, `logo` | `business_name` |

Helpers: [`src/common/utils/entity-ref.mapper.ts`](src/common/utils/entity-ref.mapper.ts) (`mapUserRef`, `mapMerchantRef`, `buildUserRefMap`).

## Nullability

- Actor not set yet (e.g. not confirmed) → **`null`** for the whole object (`confirmedBy: null`).
- Actor set but user row missing (soft-deleted) → still return `{ id, name: fallback, avatarUrl: null }` — never omit `name`.

## Checklist for new / changed responses

1. Identify every `*UserId` / `*MerchantId` / similar FK exposed for UI display.
2. Replace with a nested ref DTO (or add the nest and deprecate the bare id in the same change).
3. Document nullable refs in Swagger + `docs/*.md` (enums + nullability).
4. Batch-load refs in list endpoints (`findByIds` + `buildUserRefMap`) — no N+1.
5. Do not force the front to call `/users/:id` just to show a name.
